  <diagram id="ww3HdC16l-BEvaaz4BPS" name="API Gateway Service Diagrams">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1257" dy="23" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="827" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="6S_IK6M8-ehlRHFFc3uE-2" value="&lt;h1&gt;API Gateway Service&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The service purpose is to be a gateway for every client service which will be developed. Thanks to this service, all of the client services will have a common language which will be used for communicating with the internal system.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The service separates the clients with the inside services, thus, the clients don&#39;t know about the system&#39;s services. Furthermore, any API changes will be edited here, and won&#39;t break any other logic.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;More roles that might will taken down into more services is gate-keeping and load balancing, the service will determine which user will has access for what and will decide which instance of the service would get the request.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Use Case Diagram:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here you can see that the clients send requests in the same format to the API Gateway Service.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Class Diagram:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;spacing=5;spacingTop=-20;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="840" width="460" height="610" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
